cessful local exports such as makhana and arhar dal to various international markets. Additionally, he discussed efforts aimed at reviving traditional skills and farming practices, including natural cotton cultivation.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/give-priority-to-local-artisans-pm-modis-festive-shopping-appeal-as-diwali-approaches/articleshow/135186794.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/give-priority-to-local-artisans-pm-modis-festive-shopping-appeal-as-diwali-approaches/articleshow/135186794.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-25T14:09:31+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Yashasvi Vasistha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135186874,imgsize-78812.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Now that Nitish is no longer there': Expelled Anant Singh says has no regrets, to float own party]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/jdu-is-finished-bihar-strongman-anant-singh-to-float-own-party-after-expulsion/articleshow/135186680.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135186680.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/jdu-is-finished-bihar-strongman-anant-singh-to-float-own-party-after-expulsion/articleshow/135186680.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/jdu-is-finished-bihar-strongman-anant-singh-to-float-own-party-after-expulsion/articleshow/135186680.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-25T14:07:43+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Abhishek Mishra</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135186865,imgsize-871491.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Don't be spectator, show leadership': EAM Jaishankar to UN on terrorism, global crises]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/dont-be-spectator-show-leadership-eam-jaishankar-to-un-on-terrorism-global-crises/articleshow/135185782.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135185782.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[In his latest statements, external affairs minister S Jaishankar called for a more robust leadership from the UN to confront pressing world issues. He highlighted a significant gap in global decision-making that leaves many regions, particularly in the Global South, behind in critical areas like finance, fuel, food, and fertilizer. Emphasizing the importance of fair AI development, Jaishankar encourages strategies that ensure widespread access to its benefits, fostering international cooperation.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/dont-be-spectator-show-leadership-eam-jaishankar-to-un-on-terrorism-global-crises/articleshow/135185782.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/dont-be-spectator-show-leadership-eam-jaishankar-to-un-on-terrorism-global-crises/articleshow/135185782.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-25T12:53:54+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Aastha Jha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135185916,imgsize-91824.cms"/></item></channel></rss>